      <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140428_16562044_0124.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140428_16562044_0124&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140428_16562044_0124.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140428_16562849_0125.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;img alt=&#34;postcard-2014-20140428_16562849_0125&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;//localhost:1313/wp-content/uploads/2014/04/postcard-2014-20140428_16562849_0125.jpg&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From: M.B. Hoppler, To: Jeanette Knox Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Mailed From: Pekin, Illinois on May 31, 1911&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mrs. Nettie Chandler&lt;br&gt;
Pearl, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;May 30&lt;br&gt;
Dear Friend,&lt;br&gt;
I will drop you a card to tell you that I paid my dues twice this month. You made my reciept out for May instead of June. I paid the 3 and 6 so look at your book and still I remain yours truly,&lt;br&gt;
General Delivery M.B. Hoppler&lt;br&gt;
Pekin, Illinois&lt;/p&gt;</description>
